    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter the July 3 slate with a clear focal point in **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 rating makes him the anchor of our offense against Brady Singer. With an advantageous right-handed platoon matchup and the benefit of leading off, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our highest-upside play. Joining him at the top of the projected performance list are **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.47). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.60, allowing him to exploit the matchup against Mitch Keller with added efficiency, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a plug-and-play asset despite the respectable arm of Michael King, largely due to strong underlying metrics and a favorable dynamic platoon split.\n\nThe most notable bench decision today centers on **Nolan Schanuel**, whose 54.68 score put him on the cusp of a start. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects well, he was squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of **Cole Carrigg** (59.74), who benefits from a high park-factor boost that narrowly elevated his utility over the more traditional offensive profile of **Nolan Schanuel**. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the status of **Liam Hicks**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**; all five spots rely on pending lineups. While we have projected them into optimal order slots, any late-breaking changes\u2014particularly for **Liam Hicks** at the top of the order\u2014could shift these daily efficiency scores. Furthermore, while **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) looks strong against Austin Feltner, managers should be wary of the potential for the opposing starter to over-perform his 4.97 xERA, though the combination of a high park factor and **Heliot Ramos**'s favorable spot in the heart of the order provides a solid floor.",
